/-!
# Composition of bounds across scales, continued: a local right inverse on the infinite lattice
# and composition loss on Pauli transfer matrices

A Lean 4 / Mathlib development about proof methods for multiscale bounds. It continues the series
from Parts 1–15, and its parts are numbered 16–17. It does not import Parts 1–15: where a part uses
one of their definitions or statements, it re-defines or re-proves it. Each part was written as a
separate module and is wrapped here in its own `section`, so that its `open` commands stay local;
the namespaces are distinct, so no names clash. Each part begins with its own module docstring,
which states its main results, its scope and what it does not formalise.

| part | section | namespace | content |
|---|---|---|---|
| 16 | `Part16_JZ4` | `LemmaJZ4` | a local linear right inverse on the infinite lattice: local operators; passage of a right inverse with a uniform bound from approximating maps to the limit; kernels with bounded column sums and the Schur test; recovery through a lift; an explicit right inverse of the block-centre filter on `ℤ` and `ℤ⁴`; examples |
| 17 | `Part17_PauliComposition` | `PauliComposition` | composition loss on Pauli transfer matrices: the minimal admissible weight lemma at one step; the exact worst case, the one-shot bound and the stepwise chain, and their ordering; worked qubit examples (a rotation echo, a Clifford echo, a Bell pair with Pauli noise); applications of the general results |

## Main results

* **Part 16 (a local right inverse).** Local operators, which read finitely many inputs per
  output, are linear, depend only on the inputs they read, compose to local operators and commute
  with pointwise limits (`LocalOp.apply_add`, `LocalOp.apply_smul`, `LocalOp.apply_congr`,
  `LocalOp.comp_apply`, `LocalOp.tendsto_apply`). If linear maps `Jn n` from finitely supported
  coarse fields to fine fields converge pointwise to `J`, are eventually right inverses of a local
  operator `A`, and have uniform bounds on every finite window of their plaquette energy and of
  their column `ℓ¹` sums, then `J` is linear, `A (J y) = y`, the plaquette energy of `J y` is at
  most `C² qK y`, and `∑' i, |J y i| ≤ C1 ∑_j |y j|` (`lemmaJ_passage`). A kernel with bounded
  column sums maps finitely supported vectors to `ℓ¹`, and with a row bound as well to `ℓ²` (the
  Schur test) (`kernel_l1`, `kernel_l2`); a local operator composed with such a kernel has column
  sums bounded by the product of the two bounds (`comp_column_bound`). If `M (c j) = M (e j)` with
  `‖c j‖ ≤ C ‖M (e j)‖` and `e j → e∞` with `M e∞ = 0`, then `e j − c j` lies in the kernel of `M`
  and converges to `e∞` (`recovery_of_lift`). For the block-centre filter
  `(τ f) j = ¾ f j + ⅛ (f (j − 1) + f (j + 1))` on `ℤ`, the kernel `g j = √2 ρ^{|j|}` with
  `ρ = 2√2 − 3` satisfies `τ g = δ₀` and `∑ |g| = 2` (`tau_gk`, `hasSum_abs_gk`); for the
  tensor-product filter `T` on `ℤ⁴`, the kernel `G z = ∏_ν g (z ν)` satisfies `T G = δ₀`, its
  finite partial sums of `|G|` are at most `16`, and for every finitely supported `y`,
  `T (G ∗ y) = y`, `∑' |G ∗ y| ≤ 16 ∑ |y|` and `∑' (G ∗ y)² ≤ 256 ∑ y²` (`Tf_Gk`,
  `sum_abs_Gk_le`, `Tf_Gconv`, `Gconv_l1`, `Gconv_l2`).
* **Part 17 (composition loss on Pauli transfer matrices).** For a chain of real matrices with
  defects in a box, the change of an expectation is linear in the defects and its exact worst case
  is attained (`shift_eq`, `isGreatest_abs_shift`). The minimal admissible weight lemma, restated
  and proved (`admissible_iff`), identifies the one-shot weights as the least admissible
  site-additive weights for the composite map (`oneShot_isLeast`); the stepwise chain is
  admissible at every step and is the least such chain (`stepW_admissible`, `stepW_le`,
  `stepBound_le_chain`). Always exact worst case `≤` one-shot bound `≤` stepwise bound
  (`exactBound_le_oneShotBound`, `oneShotBound_le_stepBound`), and the three coincide when every
  column of every matrix has at most one nonzero entry (`no_loss_of_singleEntryColumns`). On the
  worked examples, with budget `1/1000` per step: in a one-qubit rotation echo (six pairs
  `R_Y(+θ), R_Y(−θ)` with `cos θ = 3/5`, observable `Z`) the exact worst case and the one-shot
  bound are `9/625` and the stepwise chain is `849821661/6103515625`, a loss ratio above `9`
  (`echo_summary`, `echo_ratio_gt_nine`); in the same circuit at `R_Y(±π/2)` (a Clifford echo) and
  in a two-qubit Bell circuit with Pauli noise, all three bounds coincide (`cliffordEcho_bounds`,
  `bell_summary`).

Part 16 ends with closed theorems that apply its results to concrete data; their docstrings say
which instances are degenerate. In Part 17 the worked examples are the main content, and its last
section applies every general result with hypotheses or parameters not used above to the data of
the examples, with all of its hypotheses discharged.

## Scope

These are results about proof methods: an abstract statement used by one proof architecture, at
Gaussian order (Part 16: a linear lift with a bound on a quadratic energy), and a worked example of
a proof-method phenomenon on qubit channels, with one two-qubit Clifford circuit as a no-loss
contrast (Part 17: chaining one site-additive estimate per step can lose, where one estimate for
the composite map does not). Lattice inputs enter only as hypotheses: in Part 16 the approximating
maps, their convergence, the right-inverse identity on the approximating lattices and the uniform
energy and column bounds are hypotheses, and the block averages, the plaquette map and the coarse
energy are arbitrary; only the block-centre filter is a concrete lattice object. In Part 17 the
entries of the transfer matrices are entered as data from the standard formulas. Nothing here is
about the Yang–Mills measure. The estimates (D) (the cube estimate `D(n, α)`) and (E) (the
existence of a nontrivial continuum limit satisfying the Osterwalder–Schrader axioms with a gap in
physical units) remain open, and so does the mass gap; nothing here addresses them.

## Conventions

* Lemma W, the minimal admissible weight lemma, names a mathematical statement; Part 17 states and
  proves it where it is used. Nothing from Parts 1–15 is imported.
* The file imports Mathlib only. It contains no `sorry`, no `admit`, no `axiom` declarations and
  no `native_decide`.
-/

/-! # Part 16: a local linear right inverse on the infinite lattice -/
section Part16_JZ4

/-!
# Part 16: a local linear right inverse on the infinite lattice

A Lean 4 / Mathlib development about proof methods. It continues the series of Parts 1–15 and does not
import them: where a statement from an earlier part is needed it is re-stated or re-proved here. The file
imports Mathlib only, and its namespace is `LemmaJZ4`.

## Setting

Fields are real-valued functions on index types: `ι` (fine links), `κ` (coarse links), `π` (fine
plaquettes). A *local operator* `A : LocalOp ι κ` assigns to every output index `k` a finite set
`A.supp k` of input indices and coefficients `A.coef k i`, and acts by
`(A f) k = ∑_{i ∈ A.supp k} A.coef k i * f i`. Finitely supported coarse fields are `κ →₀ ℝ`.

## Main results

* **Locality** (§1). Local operators are additive and homogeneous (`LocalOp.apply_add`,
  `LocalOp.apply_smul`), `(A f) k` depends only on `f` on `A.supp k` (`LocalOp.apply_congr`), a
  composite of local operators is local (`LocalOp.comp_apply`), and local operators commute with
  pointwise limits (`LocalOp.tendsto_apply`).
* **Passage of a right inverse with a uniform bound** (§2). Let `Jn n` be linear maps from finitely
  supported coarse fields to fine fields (the approximating maps, transported to the infinite lattice),
  converging pointwise to `J`. If, for every `y` and every coarse index `k`, eventually
  `(A (Jn n y)) k = y k`; if every finite window `F` of plaquettes eventually has
  `∑_{p ∈ F} ((D (Jn n y)) p)² ≤ C² qK y`; and if every finite window `F` of fine indices eventually has
  `∑_{i ∈ F} |Jn n (δ_j) i| ≤ C1`; then `J` is linear, `A (J y) = y`, `p ↦ ((D (J y)) p)²` is summable
  with sum at most `C² qK y`, and `J y` is absolutely summable with `∑' i, |J y i| ≤ C1 ∑_j |y j|`, hence
  square-summable (`lemmaJ_passage`). The pieces are `apply_eq_of_tendsto`, `energy_le_of_tendsto`,
  `l1_le_of_tendsto`, `isLinearMap_of_tendsto`, `summable_sq_of_summable_abs`.
* **Kernels with bounded columns** (§3). If `∑_{i ∈ F} |K i j| ≤ C1` for every `j` and every finite
  `F`, then `i ↦ ∑_{j ∈ S} K i j * c j` is absolutely summable with sum at most `C1 ∑_{j ∈ S} |c j|`
  (`kernel_l1`); with a row bound `R` as well, its squares sum to at most `R C1 ∑_{j ∈ S} (c j)²`
  (`kernel_l2`, the Schur test). A local operator with column sums at most `CA` composed with such a
  kernel has column sums at most `CA C1` (`comp_column_bound`).
* **Recovery through a lift with a bound in terms of the image** (§4). Let `M` be a continuous linear map,
  `e j → e∞` with `M e∞ = 0`, and let `c j` satisfy `M (c j) = M (e j)` and `‖c j‖ ≤ C ‖M (e j)‖`. Then
  `e j − c j ∈ ker M` and `e j − c j → e∞` (`recovery_of_lift`).
* **A right inverse of the block-centre filter** (§5). On `ℤ`, the filter
  `(τ f) j = ¾ f j + ⅛ (f (j − 1) + f (j + 1))` has the right-inverse kernel `g j = √2 ρ^{|j|}` with
  `ρ = 2√2 − 3`: `τ g = δ₀` (`tau_gk`), `|g j| = √2 s^{|j|}` with `s = 3 − 2√2` (`abs_gk`), and
  `∑_j |g j| = 2` (`hasSum_abs_gk`). On `ℤ⁴`, the tensor-product filter `T = τ₁τ₂τ₃τ₄` has the
  right-inverse kernel `G z = ∏_ν g (z ν)`: `T G = δ₀` (`Tf_Gk`), `|G z| = 4 s^{|z|₁}` (`abs_Gk`), every finite
  partial sum of `|G|` is at most `16` (`sum_abs_Gk_le`), and for every finitely supported `y`,
  `T (G ∗ y) = y` (`Tf_Gconv`), `∑' |G ∗ y| ≤ 16 ∑ |y|` and `∑' (G ∗ y)² ≤ 256 ∑ y²` (`Gconv_l1`,
  `Gconv_l2`).

§6 contains closed theorems that apply the results to concrete data (namespace `Example`); their
docstrings say which instances are degenerate.

## Scope

An abstract statement used by one proof architecture; lattice inputs enter only as hypotheses; nothing
about the Yang–Mills measure; (D), (E) and the mass gap remain open. In particular, the approximating maps,
their convergence, the right-inverse identity on the approximating lattices, the uniform energy bound and
the uniform column bounds of §2 are hypotheses; the block averages, the plaquette map and the coarse
energy `qK` are arbitrary local operators and functions. Only the filter of §5 is a concrete lattice
object.

## Not formalised here

The construction of the lift itself (the Whitney extension, the crossing-link embedding and their
identities), the torus versions and their periodisation, the bound `‖T⁻¹‖ ≤ 16` on all of `ℓ²` (only
finitely supported inputs are treated), the commutation of `T⁻¹` with the coarse plaquette map, and the
use of the lift in the infinite-volume passage.
-/

/-! # Part 16: a local linear right inverse on the infinite lattice -/
section Part16_LemmaJZ4

namespace LemmaJZ4

open Filter Topology Finset

noncomputable section

/-! ## 1. Local operators -/

/-- A local linear operator from real fields on `ι` to real fields on `κ`: the output index `k` reads the
finite set `supp k` of input indices, with coefficients `coef k i`. -/
structure LocalOp (ι κ : Type*) where
  /-- the input indices read by the output index `k` -/
  supp : κ → Finset ι
  /-- the coefficients -/
  coef : κ → ι → ℝ

namespace LocalOp

variable {ι κ μ : Type*}

/-- The action of a local operator: `(A f) k = ∑_{i ∈ A.supp k} A.coef k i * f i`. -/
def apply (A : LocalOp ι κ) (f : ι → ℝ) : κ → ℝ :=
  fun k => ∑ i ∈ A.supp k, A.coef k i * f i

/-- A local operator is additive: `A (f + g) = A f + A g`. -/
theorem apply_add (A : LocalOp ι κ) (f g : ι → ℝ) : A.apply (f + g) = A.apply f + A.apply g := by
  funext k
  simp [apply, mul_add, Finset.sum_add_distrib]

/-- A local operator is homogeneous: `A (c • f) = c • A f`. -/
theorem apply_smul (A : LocalOp ι κ) (c : ℝ) (f : ι → ℝ) : A.apply (c • f) = c • A.apply f := by
  funext k
  simp [apply, Finset.mul_sum, mul_left_comm]

/-- **Locality.** `(A f) k` depends only on the values of `f` on `A.supp k`. -/
theorem apply_congr (A : LocalOp ι κ) {f g : ι → ℝ} (k : κ) (h : ∀ i ∈ A.supp k, f i = g i) :
    A.apply f k = A.apply g k :=
  Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => by rw [h i hi]

/-- The composite of local operators `B ∘ A`: the output index `m` reads `⋃_{k ∈ B.supp m} A.supp k`, with
coefficients `∑_{k ∈ B.supp m} [i ∈ A.supp k] B.coef m k * A.coef k i`. -/
def comp [DecidableEq ι] (B : LocalOp κ μ) (A : LocalOp ι κ) : LocalOp ι μ where
  supp m := (B.supp m).biUnion A.supp
  coef m i := ∑ k ∈ B.supp m, if i ∈ A.supp k then B.coef m k * A.coef k i else 0

/-- **A composite of local operators is local**: `(B.comp A) f = B (A f)`. -/
theorem comp_apply [DecidableEq ι] (B : LocalOp κ μ) (A : LocalOp ι κ) (f : ι → ℝ) :
    (B.comp A).apply f = B.apply (A.apply f) := by
  funext m
  simp only [apply, comp, Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
  rw [Finset.sum_comm]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k hk => ?_
  have hsub : A.supp k ⊆ (B.supp m).biUnion A.supp := Finset.subset_biUnion_of_mem A.supp hk
  rw [← Finset.sum_subset hsub (fun i _ hi => by simp [hi])]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => ?_
  simp [hi, mul_assoc]

/-- **Pointwise convergence passes through a local operator.** If `g n i → gl i` for every `i`, then
`(A (g n)) k → (A gl) k` for every `k`. -/
theorem tendsto_apply (A : LocalOp ι κ) {g : ℕ → ι → ℝ} {gl : ι → ℝ}
    (hg : ∀ i, Tendsto (fun n => g n i) atTop (𝓝 (gl i))) (k : κ) :
    Tendsto (fun n => A.apply (g n) k) atTop (𝓝 (A.apply gl k)) :=
  tendsto_finsetSum _ fun i _ => (hg i).const_mul _

end LocalOp

/-! ## 2. Passage of a right inverse with a uniform bound -/

section Passage

variable {ι κ π : Type*}

/-- **A right-inverse identity passes to pointwise limits.** If `g n → gl` pointwise and, for every output
index `k`, eventually `(A (g n)) k = y k`, then `A gl = y`. -/
theorem apply_eq_of_tendsto (A : LocalOp ι κ) {g : ℕ → ι → ℝ} {gl : ι → ℝ}
    (hg : ∀ i, Tendsto (fun n => g n i) atTop (𝓝 (gl i))) (y : κ → ℝ)
    (hA : ∀ k, ∀ᶠ n in atTop, A.apply (g n) k = y k) : A.apply gl = y := by
  funext k
  exact tendsto_nhds_unique (A.tendsto_apply hg k)
    (tendsto_const_nhds.congr' ((hA k).mono fun n h => h.symm))

/-- **Fatou bound for a local energy.** If `g n → gl` pointwise and every finite window `F` eventually has
`∑_{p ∈ F} ((D (g n)) p)² ≤ B`, then `p ↦ ((D gl) p)²` is summable and `∑' p, ((D gl) p)² ≤ B`. -/
theorem energy_le_of_tendsto (D : LocalOp ι π) {g : ℕ → ι → ℝ} {gl : ι → ℝ}
    (hg : ∀ i, Tendsto (fun n => g n i) atTop (𝓝 (gl i))) (B : ℝ)
    (hB : ∀ F : Finset π, ∀ᶠ n in atTop, ∑ p ∈ F, D.apply (g n) p ^ 2 ≤ B) :
    Summable (fun p => D.apply gl p ^ 2) ∧ ∑' p, D.apply gl p ^ 2 ≤ B := by
  have hF : ∀ F : Finset π, ∑ p ∈ F, D.apply gl p ^ 2 ≤ B := fun F =>
    le_of_tendsto (tendsto_finsetSum F fun p _ => (D.tendsto_apply hg p).pow 2) (hB F)
  have hnn : 0 ≤ fun p => D.apply gl p ^ 2 := fun p => sq_nonneg _
  have hs : Summable (fun p => D.apply gl p ^ 2) := summable_of_sum_le hnn hF
  exact ⟨hs, hs.tsum_le_of_sum_le hF⟩

/-- **Fatou bound for `ℓ¹` windows.** If `g n → gl` pointwise and every finite window `F` eventually has
`∑_{i ∈ F} |g n i| ≤ B`, then every finite window has `∑_{i ∈ F} |gl i| ≤ B`, `i ↦ |gl i|` is summable,
and `∑' i, |gl i| ≤ B`. -/
theorem l1_le_of_tendsto {g : ℕ → ι → ℝ} {gl : ι → ℝ}
    (hg : ∀ i, Tendsto (fun n => g n i) atTop (𝓝 (gl i))) (B : ℝ)
    (hB : ∀ F : Finset ι, ∀ᶠ n in atTop, ∑ i ∈ F, |g n i| ≤ B) :
    (∀ F : Finset ι, ∑ i ∈ F, |gl i| ≤ B) ∧ Summable (fun i => |gl i|) ∧ ∑' i, |gl i| ≤ B := by
  have hF : ∀ F : Finset ι, ∑ i ∈ F, |gl i| ≤ B := fun F =>
    le_of_tendsto (tendsto_finsetSum F fun i _ => (hg i).abs) (hB F)
  have hnn : 0 ≤ fun i => |gl i| := fun i => abs_nonneg _
  have hs : Summable (fun i => |gl i|) := summable_of_sum_le hnn hF
  exact ⟨hF, hs, hs.tsum_le_of_sum_le hF⟩

/-- **Linearity passes to pointwise limits.** If linear maps `Jn n : V → (ι → ℝ)` converge pointwise to
`J`, i.e. `Jn n y i → J y i` for all `y` and `i`, then `J` is linear. -/
theorem isLinearMap_of_tendsto {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℝ V]
    (Jn : ℕ → V →ₗ[ℝ] (ι → ℝ)) (J : V → ι → ℝ)
    (hJ : ∀ y i, Tendsto (fun n => Jn n y i) atTop (𝓝 (J y i))) : IsLinearMap ℝ J := by
  constructor
  · intro y z
    funext i
    have h2 := hJ (y + z) i
    simp only [map_add, Pi.add_apply] at h2
    exact tendsto_nhds_unique h2 ((hJ y i).add (hJ z i))
  · intro c y
    funext i
    have h2 := hJ (c • y) i
    simp only [map_smul, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] at h2
    exact tendsto_nhds_unique h2 ((hJ y i).const_mul c)

/-- **`ℓ¹` implies `ℓ²`.** If `i ↦ |f i|` is summable, then `i ↦ (f i)²` is summable and
`∑' i, (f i)² ≤ (∑' i, |f i|)²`. -/
theorem summable_sq_of_summable_abs {f : ι → ℝ} (hf : Summable (fun i => |f i|)) :
    Summable (fun i => f i ^ 2) ∧ ∑' i, f i ^ 2 ≤ (∑' i, |f i|) ^ 2 := by
  set S := ∑' i, |f i| with hS
  have hle : ∀ i, |f i| ≤ S := fun i => hf.le_tsum i (fun j _ => abs_nonneg _)
  have hb : ∀ i, f i ^ 2 ≤ S * |f i| := fun i => by
    rw [← sq_abs, sq]
    exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hle i) (abs_nonneg _)
  have hs : Summable (fun i => S * |f i|) := hf.mul_left S
  have hs2 : Summable (fun i => f i ^ 2) := Summable.of_nonneg_of_le (fun i => sq_nonneg _) hb hs
  refine ⟨hs2, ?_⟩
  calc ∑' i, f i ^ 2 ≤ ∑' i, S * |f i| := hs2.tsum_le_tsum hb hs
    _ = S ^ 2 := by rw [hf.tsum_mul_left S, ← hS, sq]

end Passage

/-! ## 3. Kernels with bounded columns -/

section Kernel

variable {ι κ μ : Type*}

/-- **A kernel with bounded column `ℓ¹` norms maps finitely supported vectors to `ℓ¹`.** Let
`K : ι → κ → ℝ` satisfy `∑_{i ∈ F} |K i j| ≤ C1` for every `j` and every finite set `F`. Then for every
finite set `S` and coefficients `c`, the vector `i ↦ ∑_{j ∈ S} K i j * c j` is absolutely summable with
`∑' i, |∑_{j ∈ S} K i j * c j| ≤ C1 ∑_{j ∈ S} |c j|`. -/
theorem kernel_l1 (K : ι → κ → ℝ) (C1 : ℝ) (hK : ∀ j (F : Finset ι), ∑ i ∈ F, |K i j| ≤ C1)
    (S : Finset κ) (c : κ → ℝ) :
    Summable (fun i => |∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j|) ∧
      ∑' i, |∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j| ≤ C1 * ∑ j ∈ S, |c j| := by
  have hF : ∀ F : Finset ι, ∑ i ∈ F, |∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j| ≤ C1 * ∑ j ∈ S, |c j| := by
    intro F
    calc ∑ i ∈ F, |∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j| ≤ ∑ i ∈ F, ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * |c j| := by
          refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun i _ => ?_
          refine (Finset.abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans (le_of_eq ?_)
          simp [abs_mul]
      _ = ∑ j ∈ S, (∑ i ∈ F, |K i j|) * |c j| := by
          rw [Finset.sum_comm]
          simp [Finset.sum_mul]
      _ ≤ ∑ j ∈ S, C1 * |c j| :=
          Finset.sum_le_sum fun j _ => mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hK j F) (abs_nonneg _)
      _ = C1 * ∑ j ∈ S, |c j| := by rw [Finset.mul_sum]
  have hnn : 0 ≤ fun i => |∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j| := fun i => abs_nonneg _
  have hs := summable_of_sum_le hnn hF
  exact ⟨hs, hs.tsum_le_of_sum_le hF⟩

/-- Weighted Cauchy–Schwarz: for `a ≥ 0`, `(∑ a b)² ≤ (∑ a) (∑ a b²)`. -/
theorem sq_sum_le_weighted (S : Finset κ) (a b : κ → ℝ) (ha : ∀ j, 0 ≤ a j) :
    (∑ j ∈ S, a j * b j) ^ 2 ≤ (∑ j ∈ S, a j) * ∑ j ∈ S, a j * b j ^ 2 := by
  have h := Finset.sum_mul_sq_le_sq_mul_sq S (fun j => Real.sqrt (a j)) (fun j => Real.sqrt (a j) * b j)
  have e1 : ∀ j, Real.sqrt (a j) * (Real.sqrt (a j) * b j) = a j * b j := fun j => by
    rw [← mul_assoc, Real.mul_self_sqrt (ha j)]
  have e2 : ∀ j, Real.sqrt (a j) ^ 2 = a j := fun j => Real.sq_sqrt (ha j)
  have e3 : ∀ j, (Real.sqrt (a j) * b j) ^ 2 = a j * b j ^ 2 := fun j => by
    rw [mul_pow, Real.sq_sqrt (ha j)]
  simpa only [e1, e2, e3] using h

/-- **Schur test on finite windows.** Let `S` be a finite set of coarse indices, and let `K` have row sums
`∑_{j ∈ S} |K i j| ≤ R` for every `i` (with `R ≥ 0`) and column sums `∑_{i ∈ F} |K i j| ≤ C1` for every `j`
and every finite set `F`. Then for coefficients `c`, the vector `i ↦ ∑_{j ∈ S} K i j * c j` is
square-summable with `∑' i, (∑_{j ∈ S} K i j * c j)² ≤ R C1 ∑_{j ∈ S} (c j)²`. -/
theorem kernel_l2 (K : ι → κ → ℝ) (R C1 : ℝ) (hR0 : 0 ≤ R) (S : Finset κ) (c : κ → ℝ)
    (hR : ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| ≤ R) (hK : ∀ j (F : Finset ι), ∑ i ∈ F, |K i j| ≤ C1) :
    Summable (fun i => (∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j) ^ 2) ∧
      ∑' i, (∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j) ^ 2 ≤ R * C1 * ∑ j ∈ S, c j ^ 2 := by
  have hpt : ∀ i, (∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j) ^ 2 ≤ R * ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * c j ^ 2 := by
    intro i
    have h1 : |∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j| ≤ ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * |c j| := by
      refine (Finset.abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans (le_of_eq ?_)
      simp [abs_mul]
    have h2 := sq_sum_le_weighted S (fun j => |K i j|) (fun j => |c j|) (fun j => abs_nonneg _)
    have h3 : 0 ≤ ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * |c j| ^ 2 :=
      Finset.sum_nonneg fun j _ => mul_nonneg (abs_nonneg _) (sq_nonneg _)
    calc (∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j) ^ 2 = |∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j| ^ 2 := (sq_abs _).symm
      _ ≤ (∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * |c j|) ^ 2 := pow_le_pow_left₀ (abs_nonneg _) h1 2
      _ ≤ (∑ j ∈ S, |K i j|) * ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * |c j| ^ 2 := h2
      _ ≤ R * ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * |c j| ^ 2 := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hR i) h3
      _ = R * ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * c j ^ 2 := by simp [sq_abs]
  have hF : ∀ F : Finset ι, ∑ i ∈ F, (∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j) ^ 2 ≤ R * C1 * ∑ j ∈ S, c j ^ 2 := by
    intro F
    calc ∑ i ∈ F, (∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j) ^ 2 ≤ ∑ i ∈ F, R * ∑ j ∈ S, |K i j| * c j ^ 2 :=
          Finset.sum_le_sum fun i _ => hpt i
      _ = R * ∑ j ∈ S, (∑ i ∈ F, |K i j|) * c j ^ 2 := by
          rw [← Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_comm]
          simp [Finset.sum_mul]
      _ ≤ R * ∑ j ∈ S, C1 * c j ^ 2 :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left
            (Finset.sum_le_sum fun j _ => mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hK j F) (sq_nonneg _)) hR0
      _ = R * C1 * ∑ j ∈ S, c j ^ 2 := by rw [← Finset.mul_sum, mul_assoc]
  have hnn : 0 ≤ fun i => (∑ j ∈ S, K i j * c j) ^ 2 := fun i => sq_nonneg _
  have hs := summable_of_sum_le hnn hF
  exact ⟨hs, hs.tsum_le_of_sum_le hF⟩

/-- **Column sums of a local operator composed with a kernel.** Let `A : LocalOp μ ι` have column sums
`∑_{i ∈ F, m ∈ A.supp i} |A.coef i m| ≤ CA` (with `CA ≥ 0`) for every `m` and every finite `F`, and let
`K : μ → κ → ℝ` have column sums `∑_{m ∈ F} |K m j| ≤ C1`. Then the composite kernel
`(i, j) ↦ (A (K · j)) i` has column sums at most `CA C1` over every finite set. -/
theorem comp_column_bound [DecidableEq μ] (A : LocalOp μ ι) (K : μ → κ → ℝ)
    (CA C1 : ℝ) (hCA : 0 ≤ CA)
    (hA : ∀ m (F : Finset ι), ∑ i ∈ F.filter (fun i => m ∈ A.supp i), |A.coef i m| ≤ CA)
    (hK : ∀ j (F : Finset μ), ∑ m ∈ F, |K m j| ≤ C1) (j : κ) (F : Finset ι) :
    ∑ i ∈ F, |A.apply (fun m => K m j) i| ≤ CA * C1 := by
  show ∑ i ∈ F, |∑ m ∈ A.supp i, A.coef i m * K m j| ≤ CA * C1
  calc ∑ i ∈ F, |∑ m ∈ A.supp i, A.coef i m * K m j|
        ≤ ∑ i ∈ F, ∑ m ∈ A.supp i, |A.coef i m| * |K m j| := by
          refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun i _ => ?_
          refine (Finset.abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans (le_of_eq ?_)
          simp [abs_mul]
    _ = ∑ m ∈ F.biUnion A.supp, ∑ i ∈ F.filter (fun i => m ∈ A.supp i), |A.coef i m| * |K m j| := by
          refine Finset.sum_comm' fun i m => ?_
          simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_biUnion]
          constructor
          · rintro ⟨hi, hm⟩
            exact ⟨⟨hi, hm⟩, i, hi, hm⟩
          · rintro ⟨⟨hi, hm⟩, _⟩
            exact ⟨hi, hm⟩
    _ = ∑ m ∈ F.biUnion A.supp, (∑ i ∈ F.filter (fun i => m ∈ A.supp i), |A.coef i m|) * |K m j| := by
          simp [Finset.sum_mul]
    _ ≤ ∑ m ∈ F.biUnion A.supp, CA * |K m j| :=
          Finset.sum_le_sum fun m _ => mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hA m F) (abs_nonneg _)
    _ = CA * ∑ m ∈ F.biUnion A.supp, |K m j| := by rw [Finset.mul_sum]
    _ ≤ CA * C1 := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hK j _) hCA

end Kernel

/-! ### The passage theorem -/

/-- **Passage of a local linear right inverse with a uniform bound to the infinite lattice.** Let
`A : LocalOp ι κ` (the block averages) and `D : LocalOp ι π` (the plaquette map) be local operators, `qK` a
function on finitely supported coarse fields (the coarse energy), and `C, C1` constants. Let
`Jn n : (κ →₀ ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (ι → ℝ)` be linear maps converging pointwise to `J`. Assume:
* for every `y` and every coarse index `k`, eventually `(A (Jn n y)) k = y k`;
* for every `y` and every finite window `F` of plaquettes, eventually
  `∑_{p ∈ F} ((D (Jn n y)) p)² ≤ C² qK y`;
* for every coarse index `j` and every finite window `F` of fine indices, eventually
  `∑_{i ∈ F} |Jn n (δ_j) i| ≤ C1`, where `δ_j = Finsupp.single j 1`.

Then `J` is linear; `A (J y) = y`; `p ↦ ((D (J y)) p)²` is summable with sum at most `C² qK y`; `J y` is
absolutely summable with `∑' i, |J y i| ≤ C1 ∑_{j ∈ supp y} |y j|`; and `J y` is square-summable with
`∑' i, (J y i)² ≤ (C1 ∑_{j ∈ supp y} |y j|)²`. -/
theorem lemmaJ_passage {ι κ π : Type*} (A : LocalOp ι κ) (D : LocalOp ι π) (qK : (κ →₀ ℝ) → ℝ)
    (C C1 : ℝ) (Jn : ℕ → (κ →₀ ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (ι → ℝ)) (J : (κ →₀ ℝ) → ι → ℝ)
    (hconv : ∀ y i, Tendsto (fun n => Jn n y i) atTop (𝓝 (J y i)))
    (hA : ∀ y k, ∀ᶠ n in atTop, A.apply (Jn n y) k = y k)
    (hD : ∀ y (F : Finset π), ∀ᶠ n in atTop, ∑ p ∈ F, D.apply (Jn n y) p ^ 2 ≤ C ^ 2 * qK y)
    (hl1 : ∀ j (F : Finset ι), ∀ᶠ n in atTop, ∑ i ∈ F, |Jn n (Finsupp.single j 1) i| ≤ C1) :
    IsLinearMap ℝ J ∧
      (∀ y, A.apply (J y) = ⇑y) ∧
      (∀ y, Summable (fun p => D.apply (J y) p ^ 2) ∧ ∑' p, D.apply (J y) p ^ 2 ≤ C ^ 2 * qK y) ∧
      (∀ y, Summable (fun i => |J y i|) ∧ ∑' i, |J y i| ≤ C1 * ∑ j ∈ y.support, |y j|) ∧
      (∀ y, Summable (fun i => J y i ^ 2) ∧
        ∑' i, J y i ^ 2 ≤ (C1 * ∑ j ∈ y.support, |y j|) ^ 2) := by
  have hlin := isLinearMap_of_tendsto Jn J hconv
  set Jl : (κ →₀ ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (ι → ℝ) := IsLinearMap.mk' J hlin with hJl
  have hexp : ∀ y i, J y i = ∑ j ∈ y.support, J (Finsupp.single j 1) i * y j := by
    intro y i
    have h : Jl y = ∑ j ∈ y.support, y j • Jl (Finsupp.single j 1) := by
      conv_lhs => rw [← Finsupp.sum_single y]
      rw [Finsupp.sum, map_sum]
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
      rw [show Finsupp.single j (y j) = y j • Finsupp.single j 1 from
        (Finsupp.smul_single_one j (y j)).symm, map_smul]
    have h' := congrFun h i
    simp only [hJl, IsLinearMap.mk'_apply, Finset.sum_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] at h'
    rw [h']
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => mul_comm _ _
  have hcol : ∀ j (F : Finset ι), ∑ i ∈ F, |J (Finsupp.single j 1) i| ≤ C1 := fun j =>
    (l1_le_of_tendsto (fun i => hconv (Finsupp.single j 1) i) C1 (hl1 j)).1
  have hl1y : ∀ y : κ →₀ ℝ,
      Summable (fun i => |J y i|) ∧ ∑' i, |J y i| ≤ C1 * ∑ j ∈ y.support, |y j| := by
    intro y
    have h := kernel_l1 (fun i j => J (Finsupp.single j 1) i) C1 hcol y.support y
    have e : (fun i => |∑ j ∈ y.support, J (Finsupp.single j 1) i * y j|) = fun i => |J y i| := by
      funext i
      rw [hexp y i]
    beta_reduce at h
    rw [e] at h
    exact h
  refine ⟨hlin, fun y => apply_eq_of_tendsto A (hconv y) y (hA y),
    fun y => energy_le_of_tendsto D (hconv y) _ (hD y), hl1y, fun y => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨hs, hle⟩ := hl1y y
  obtain ⟨hs2, hle2⟩ := summable_sq_of_summable_abs hs
  exact ⟨hs2, hle2.trans (pow_le_pow_left₀ (tsum_nonneg fun i => abs_nonneg _) hle 2)⟩

/-! ## 4. Recovery through a lift with a bound in terms of the image -/

/-- **Recovery through a lift.** Let `M : E →L[ℝ] G` be a continuous linear map between real normed
spaces, `e j → e∞` with `M e∞ = 0`, and let `c j` satisfy `M (c j) = M (e j)` and
`‖c j‖ ≤ C ‖M (e j)‖`. Then `M (e j − c j) = 0` for every `j`, and `e j − c j → e∞`. -/
theorem recovery_of_lift {E G : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]
    [NormedAddCommGroup G] [NormedSpace ℝ G] (M : E →L[ℝ] G) (C : ℝ) (e c : ℕ → E) (einf : E)
    (he : Tendsto e atTop (𝓝 einf)) (hM0 : M einf = 0) (hMc : ∀ j, M (c j) = M (e j))
    (hc : ∀ j, ‖c j‖ ≤ C * ‖M (e j)‖) :
    (∀ j, M (e j - c j) = 0) ∧ Tendsto (fun j => e j - c j) atTop (𝓝 einf) := by
  refine ⟨fun j => by rw [map_sub, hMc, sub_self], ?_⟩
  have hδ : Tendsto (fun j => M (e j)) atTop (𝓝 0) := by
    have h := (M.continuous.tendsto einf).comp he
    rw [hM0] at h
    exact h
  have hc0 : Tendsto c atTop (𝓝 0) := by
    refine squeeze_zero_norm hc ?_
    simpa using hδ.norm.const_mul C
  simpa using he.sub hc0

/-! ## 5. A right inverse of the block-centre filter on `ℤ` and on `ℤ⁴` -/

section Filter

/-- `√2 ^ 2 = 2`. -/
theorem sqrt_two_sq : Real.sqrt 2 ^ 2 = 2 := Real.sq_sqrt (by norm_num)

/-- `7/5 < √2`. -/
theorem sqrt_two_gt : (7 / 5 : ℝ) < Real.sqrt 2 := by
  nlinarith [sqrt_two_sq, Real.sqrt_nonneg 2]

/-- `√2 < 3/2`. -/
theorem sqrt_two_lt : Real.sqrt 2 < 3 / 2 := by
  nlinarith [sqrt_two_sq, Real.sqrt_nonneg 2]

/-- `ρ = 2√2 − 3`. -/
def rho : ℝ := 2 * Real.sqrt 2 - 3

/-- `s = 3 − 2√2`, the decay factor per lattice step. -/
def sdec : ℝ := 3 - 2 * Real.sqrt 2

/-- `ρ² + 6ρ + 1 = 0`. -/
theorem rho_quad : rho ^ 2 + 6 * rho + 1 = 0 := by
  unfold rho
  linear_combination (4 : ℝ) * sqrt_two_sq

/-- `0 < s`. -/
theorem sdec_pos : 0 < sdec := by
  unfold sdec
  linarith [sqrt_two_lt]

/-- `s < 1`. -/
theorem sdec_lt_one : sdec < 1 := by
  unfold sdec
  linarith [sqrt_two_gt]

/-- `|ρ| = s`. -/
theorem abs_rho : |rho| = sdec := by
  have h : rho = -sdec := by
    unfold rho sdec
    ring
  rw [h, abs_neg, abs_of_pos sdec_pos]

/-- The one-dimensional kernel `g j = √2 ρ^{|j|}`. -/
def gk (j : ℤ) : ℝ := Real.sqrt 2 * rho ^ j.natAbs

/-- The one-dimensional filter `(τ f) j = ¾ f j + ⅛ (f (j − 1) + f (j + 1))`. -/
def tau (f : ℤ → ℝ) (j : ℤ) : ℝ := 3 / 4 * f j + 1 / 8 * (f (j - 1) + f (j + 1))

/-- **`g` inverts `τ`**: `τ g = δ₀`. -/
theorem tau_gk (j : ℤ) : tau gk j = if j = 0 then 1 else 0 := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl | rfl⟩ := Int.eq_nat_or_neg j
  · rcases m with _ | k
    · simp [tau, gk, rho]
      linear_combination (1 / 2 : ℝ) * sqrt_two_sq
    · have h1 : ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 1 = ((k : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast; ring
      have h2 : ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1 = ((k + 2 : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast; ring
      have h3 : ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by omega
      simp only [tau, gk, h1, h2, Int.natAbs_natCast, if_neg h3]
      linear_combination (Real.sqrt 2 * rho ^ k / 8) * rho_quad
  · rcases m with _ | k
    · simp [tau, gk, rho]
      linear_combination (1 / 2 : ℝ) * sqrt_two_sq
    · have h1 : -((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 1 = -((k + 2 : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast; ring
      have h2 : -((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1 = -((k : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast; ring
      have h3 : -((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by omega
      simp only [tau, gk, h1, h2, Int.natAbs_neg, Int.natAbs_natCast, if_neg h3]
      linear_combination (Real.sqrt 2 * rho ^ k / 8) * rho_quad

/-- **Decay of `g`**: `|g j| = √2 s^{|j|}`. -/
theorem abs_gk (j : ℤ) : |gk j| = Real.sqrt 2 * sdec ^ j.natAbs := by
  rw [gk, abs_mul, abs_pow, abs_rho, abs_of_pos (Real.sqrt_pos.2 two_pos)]

/-- **`ℓ¹` norm of `g`**: `∑_{j ∈ ℤ} |g j| = 2`. -/
theorem hasSum_abs_gk : HasSum (fun j : ℤ => |gk j|) 2 := by
  have hg := hasSum_geometric_of_lt_one sdec_pos.le sdec_lt_one
  have h1 : HasSum (fun n : ℕ => |gk (n : ℤ)|) (Real.sqrt 2 * (1 - sdec)⁻¹) := by
    have e : (fun n : ℕ => |gk (n : ℤ)|) = fun n => Real.sqrt 2 * sdec ^ n := by
      funext n
      rw [abs_gk, Int.natAbs_natCast]
    rw [e]
    exact hg.mul_left _
  have h2 : HasSum (fun n : ℕ => |gk (-((n : ℤ) + 1))|) (Real.sqrt 2 * sdec * (1 - sdec)⁻¹) := by
    have e : (fun n : ℕ => |gk (-((n : ℤ) + 1))|) = fun n => Real.sqrt 2 * sdec * sdec ^ n := by
      funext n
      have hn : (-((n : ℤ) + 1)).natAbs = n + 1 := by
        rw [Int.natAbs_neg, show (n : ℤ) + 1 = ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) by push_cast; ring,
          Int.natAbs_natCast]
      rw [abs_gk, hn, pow_succ]
      ring
    rw [e]
    exact hg.mul_left _
  have h := HasSum.of_nat_of_neg_add_one (f := fun j : ℤ => |gk j|) h1 h2
  have hne : (1 - sdec) ≠ 0 := by linarith [sdec_lt_one]
  have key : Real.sqrt 2 * (1 + sdec) = 2 * (1 - sdec) := by
    unfold sdec
    linear_combination (-2 : ℝ) * sqrt_two_sq
  have hval : Real.sqrt 2 * (1 - sdec)⁻¹ + Real.sqrt 2 * sdec * (1 - sdec)⁻¹ = 2 := by
    calc Real.sqrt 2 * (1 - sdec)⁻¹ + Real.sqrt 2 * sdec * (1 - sdec)⁻¹
          = Real.sqrt 2 * (1 + sdec) * (1 - sdec)⁻¹ := by ring
      _ = 2 * (1 - sdec) * (1 - sdec)⁻¹ := by rw [key]
      _ = 2 := mul_inv_cancel_right₀ hne 2
  rwa [hval] at h

/-- Every finite partial sum of `|g|` is at most `2`. -/
theorem sum_abs_gk_le (F : Finset ℤ) : ∑ j ∈ F, |gk j| ≤ 2 :=
  sum_le_hasSum F (fun _ _ => abs_nonneg _) hasSum_abs_gk

/-- Sites of `ℤ⁴`. -/
abbrev Z4 : Type := Fin 4 → ℤ

/-- The four-dimensional kernel `G z = ∏_ν g (z ν)`. -/
def Gk (z : Z4) : ℝ := ∏ ν, gk (z ν)

/-- The filter weights: `w 0 = 3/4` and `w a = 1/8` otherwise (used for `a = ±1`). -/
def wf (a : ℤ) : ℝ := if a = 0 then 3 / 4 else 1 / 8

/-- The three-point stencil `{−1, 0, 1}`. -/
def st : Finset ℤ := {-1, 0, 1}

/-- The tensor-product filter `T = τ₁τ₂τ₃τ₄` on `ℤ⁴`, written as one stencil:
`(T f) z = ∑_{e ∈ {−1, 0, 1}⁴} (∏_ν w (e ν)) f (z + e)`. -/
def Tf (f : Z4 → ℝ) (z : Z4) : ℝ :=
  ∑ e ∈ Fintype.piFinset (fun _ : Fin 4 => st), (∏ ν, wf (e ν)) * f (z + e)

/-- `τ` is the one-dimensional stencil with weights `w`. -/
theorem tau_eq_stencil (f : ℤ → ℝ) (j : ℤ) : tau f j = ∑ a ∈ st, wf a * f (j + a) := by
  simp [tau, st, wf, sub_eq_add_neg]
  ring

/-- `T` acts on product functions factor by factor. -/
theorem Tf_prod (h : Fin 4 → ℤ → ℝ) (z : Z4) :
    Tf (fun x => ∏ ν, h ν (x ν)) z = ∏ ν, ∑ a ∈ st, wf a * h ν (z ν + a) := by
  rw [Finset.prod_univ_sum]
  unfold Tf
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun e _ => ?_
  simp only [Pi.add_apply, Finset.prod_mul_distrib]

/-- **`G` inverts `T`**: `T G = δ₀` on `ℤ⁴`. -/
theorem Tf_Gk (z : Z4) : Tf Gk z = if z = 0 then 1 else 0 := by
  have h := Tf_prod (fun _ => gk) z
  have hfac : ∀ ν, ∑ a ∈ st, wf a * gk (z ν + a) = if z ν = 0 then 1 else 0 := fun ν =>
    (tau_eq_stencil gk (z ν)).symm.trans (tau_gk (z ν))
  have hG : (fun x : Z4 => ∏ ν, (fun _ : Fin 4 => gk) ν (x ν)) = Gk := rfl
  rw [hG] at h
  rw [h, Finset.prod_congr rfl fun ν _ => hfac ν]
  by_cases hz : z = 0
  · subst hz
    simp
  · rw [if_neg hz]
    obtain ⟨ν, hν⟩ := Function.ne_iff.mp hz
    have hν' : z ν ≠ 0 := hν
    exact Finset.prod_eq_zero (Finset.mem_univ ν) (by simp [hν'])

/-- **Decay of `G`**: `|G z| = 4 s^{|z|₁}` with `|z|₁ = ∑_ν |z ν|`. -/
theorem abs_Gk (z : Z4) : |Gk z| = 4 * sdec ^ (∑ ν, (z ν).natAbs) := by
  rw [Gk, Finset.abs_prod]
  simp_rw [abs_gk]
  rw [Finset.prod_mul_distrib, Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum, Finset.prod_const, Finset.card_univ,
    Fintype.card_fin]
  congr 1
  rw [show (4 : ℕ) = 2 * 2 from rfl, pow_mul, sqrt_two_sq]
  norm_num

/-- **`ℓ¹` bound for `G`**: every finite partial sum of `|G|` is at most `2⁴ = 16`. -/
theorem sum_abs_Gk_le (F : Finset Z4) : ∑ z ∈ F, |Gk z| ≤ 16 := by
  classical
  set t : Fin 4 → Finset ℤ := fun ν => F.image (fun z => z ν) with ht
  have hsub : F ⊆ Fintype.piFinset t := fun z hz =>
    Fintype.mem_piFinset.2 fun ν => Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hz
  calc ∑ z ∈ F, |Gk z| ≤ ∑ z ∈ Fintype.piFinset t, |Gk z| :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg hsub fun _ _ _ => abs_nonneg _
    _ = ∏ ν, ∑ a ∈ t ν, |gk a| := by
        rw [Finset.prod_univ_sum]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun z _ => ?_
        rw [Gk, Finset.abs_prod]
    _ ≤ ∏ _ν : Fin 4, (2 : ℝ) :=
        Finset.prod_le_prod (fun ν _ => Finset.sum_nonneg fun a _ => abs_nonneg _)
          fun ν _ => sum_abs_gk_le _
    _ = 16 := by norm_num [Finset.prod_const]

/-- Column sums of the translation kernel `(z, z') ↦ G (z − z')` are at most `16`. -/
theorem sum_abs_Gk_sub_le (z' : Z4) (F : Finset Z4) : ∑ z ∈ F, |Gk (z - z')| ≤ 16 := by
  classical
  have hinj : Set.InjOn (fun z : Z4 => z - z') F := fun a _ b _ h => sub_left_injective h
  have h := sum_abs_Gk_le (F.image (fun z => z - z'))
  rwa [Finset.sum_image hinj] at h

/-- Row sums of the translation kernel `(z, z') ↦ G (z − z')` are at most `16`. -/
theorem sum_abs_Gk_sub_le' (z : Z4) (S : Finset Z4) : ∑ z' ∈ S, |Gk (z - z')| ≤ 16 := by
  classical
  have hinj : Set.InjOn (fun z' : Z4 => z - z') S := fun a _ b _ h => sub_right_injective h
  have h := sum_abs_Gk_le (S.image (fun z' => z - z'))
  rwa [Finset.sum_image hinj] at h

/-- The convolution `(G ∗ y) z = ∑_{z' ∈ supp y} G (z − z') y z'` of `G` with a finitely supported
field `y` on `ℤ⁴`. -/
def Gconv (y : Z4 →₀ ℝ) (z : Z4) : ℝ := ∑ z' ∈ y.support, Gk (z - z') * y z'

/-- **`G ∗` is a right inverse of `T` on finitely supported fields**: `T (G ∗ y) = y`. -/
theorem Tf_Gconv (y : Z4 →₀ ℝ) : Tf (Gconv y) = ⇑y := by
  funext z
  have h1 : Tf (Gconv y) z = ∑ z' ∈ y.support, Tf Gk (z - z') * y z' := by
    unfold Tf Gconv
    simp_rw [Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_mul]
    rw [Finset.sum_comm]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun z' _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun e _ => ?_
    rw [add_sub_right_comm]
    ring
  rw [h1]
  simp_rw [Tf_Gk, sub_eq_zero, ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul]
  rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq]
  split_ifs with h
  · rfl
  · simp only [Finsupp.mem_support_iff, not_not] at h
    exact h.symm

/-- **`ℓ¹` bound for `G ∗`**: for finitely supported `y`, `G ∗ y` is absolutely summable with
`∑' z, |(G ∗ y) z| ≤ 16 ∑_{z'} |y z'|`. -/
theorem Gconv_l1 (y : Z4 →₀ ℝ) :
    Summable (fun z => |Gconv y z|) ∧ ∑' z, |Gconv y z| ≤ 16 * ∑ z' ∈ y.support, |y z'| :=
  kernel_l1 (fun z z' => Gk (z - z')) 16 (fun z' F => sum_abs_Gk_sub_le z' F) y.support y

/-- **`ℓ²` bound for `G ∗`**: for finitely supported `y`, `∑' z, ((G ∗ y) z)² ≤ 256 ∑_{z'} (y z')²`,
i.e. `‖G ∗ y‖ ≤ 16 ‖y‖` on finitely supported fields. Here `G ∗ y` is a right inverse of `T` applied to `y`
(`Tf_Gconv`); that it equals `T⁻¹ y`, which needs injectivity of `T` on `ℓ²`, is not formalised. -/
theorem Gconv_l2 (y : Z4 →₀ ℝ) :
    Summable (fun z => Gconv y z ^ 2) ∧
      ∑' z, Gconv y z ^ 2 ≤ 16 * 16 * ∑ z' ∈ y.support, y z' ^ 2 :=
  kernel_l2 (fun z z' => Gk (z - z')) 16 16 (by norm_num) y.support y
    (fun z => sum_abs_Gk_sub_le' z y.support) (fun z' F => sum_abs_Gk_sub_le z' F)

end Filter

/-! ## 6. Examples -/

namespace Example

/-- Block averages on `ℤ` with blocks `{2w, 2w + 1}`: `(A f) w = ½ (f (2w) + f (2w + 1))`. -/
def blockAvg : LocalOp ℤ ℤ := ⟨fun w => {2 * w, 2 * w + 1}, fun _ _ => 1 / 2⟩

/-- The difference operator on `ℤ`: `(D f) p = f (p + 1) − f p`. -/
def diffOp : LocalOp ℤ ℤ := ⟨fun p => {p, p + 1}, fun p i => if i = p then -1 else 1⟩

/-- The identity of `ℤ`, as a local operator. -/
def idOp : LocalOp ℤ ℤ := ⟨fun k => {k}, fun _ _ => 1⟩

/-- The filter `τ` of §5, as a local operator on `ℤ`. -/
def tauOp : LocalOp ℤ ℤ := ⟨fun i => {i - 1, i, i + 1}, fun i m => if m = i then 3 / 4 else 1 / 8⟩

/-- `(A f) w = (f (2w) + f (2w + 1)) / 2` for the block averages. -/
theorem blockAvg_apply (f : ℤ → ℝ) (w : ℤ) :
    blockAvg.apply f w = (f (2 * w) + f (2 * w + 1)) / 2 := by
  have h : 2 * w ≠ 2 * w + 1 := by omega
  simp only [LocalOp.apply, blockAvg, Finset.sum_pair h]
  ring

/-- `(D f) p = f (p + 1) − f p` for the difference operator. -/
theorem diffOp_apply (f : ℤ → ℝ) (p : ℤ) : diffOp.apply f p = f (p + 1) - f p := by
  have h : p ≠ p + 1 := by omega
  have h' : p + 1 ≠ p := by omega
  simp only [LocalOp.apply, diffOp, Finset.sum_pair h, if_neg h', ↓reduceIte]
  ring

/-- The identity operator acts as the identity. -/
theorem idOp_apply (f : ℤ → ℝ) (k : ℤ) : idOp.apply f k = f k := by
  simp [LocalOp.apply, idOp]

/-- The local operator `tauOp` acts as the filter `τ`. -/
theorem tauOp_apply (f : ℤ → ℝ) (i : ℤ) : tauOp.apply f i = tau f i := by
  have h1 : i - 1 ∉ ({i, i + 1} : Finset ℤ) := by
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]
    omega
  have h2 : i ∉ ({i + 1} : Finset ℤ) := by
    simp only [Finset.mem_singleton]
    omega
  have e1 : i - 1 ≠ i := by omega
  have e2 : i + 1 ≠ i := by omega
  simp only [LocalOp.apply, tauOp, Finset.sum_insert h1, Finset.sum_insert h2, Finset.sum_singleton,
    if_neg e1, if_neg e2, ↓reduceIte, tau]
  ring

/-- A sum of nonnegative terms that vanish off `T` is at most the sum over `T`. -/
theorem sum_le_of_vanish {α : Type*} [DecidableEq α] (f : α → ℝ) (T : Finset α)
    (hf0 : ∀ p, 0 ≤ f p) (hT : ∀ p ∉ T, f p = 0) (F : Finset α) :
    ∑ p ∈ F, f p ≤ ∑ p ∈ T, f p :=
  calc ∑ p ∈ F, f p = ∑ p ∈ F ∩ T, f p :=
        (Finset.sum_subset (show F ∩ T ⊆ F from Finset.inter_subset_left)
          (fun p hpF hp => hT p (fun hpT => hp (Finset.mem_inter.2 ⟨hpF, hpT⟩)))).symm
    _ ≤ ∑ p ∈ T, f p :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg (show F ∩ T ⊆ T from Finset.inter_subset_right)
          (fun p _ _ => hf0 p)

/-! ### A varying sequence of right inverses of the block averages -/

/-- The block-constant lift of `δ₀`: `1` on the fine sites `0, 1` and `0` elsewhere. -/
def liftEx (i : ℤ) : ℝ := if i = 0 ∨ i = 1 then 1 else 0

/-- A bump with zero block averages: `1` at `0`, `−1` at `1`, `0` elsewhere. -/
def bumpEx (i : ℤ) : ℝ := if i = 0 then 1 else if i = 1 then -1 else 0

/-- The perturbed lift `lift + ε · bump`. -/
def gE (ε : ℝ) (i : ℤ) : ℝ := liftEx i + ε * bumpEx i

/-- The approximants `g n = lift + (n + 1)⁻¹ · bump`. -/
def gEx (n : ℕ) : ℤ → ℝ := gE (1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1))

/-- The approximants converge pointwise to the block-constant lift. -/
theorem gEx_tendsto (i : ℤ) : Tendsto (fun n => gEx n i) atTop (𝓝 (liftEx i)) := by
  have h := (tendsto_one_div_add_atTop_nhds_zero_nat (𝕜 := ℝ)).mul_const (bumpEx i)
  have h2 := (tendsto_const_nhds (x := liftEx i)).add h
  simpa [gEx, gE] using h2

/-- For every `ε`, the block averages of `lift + ε · bump` are `δ₀`. -/
theorem gE_blockAvg (ε : ℝ) (k : ℤ) :
    blockAvg.apply (gE ε) k = (Finsupp.single (0 : ℤ) (1 : ℝ)) k := by
  rw [blockAvg_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
  by_cases hk : k = 0
  · subst hk
    norm_num [gE, liftEx, bumpEx]
    ring
  · have h1 : 2 * k ≠ 0 := by omega
    have h2 : 2 * k ≠ 1 := by omega
    have h3 : 2 * k + 1 ≠ 0 := by omega
    have h4 : 2 * k + 1 ≠ 1 := by omega
    have h5 : (0 : ℤ) ≠ k := fun h => hk h.symm
    simp [gE, liftEx, bumpEx, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5]

/-- For `0 ≤ ε ≤ 1`, every finite window of the difference energy of `lift + ε · bump` is at most `8`. -/
theorem gE_energy (ε : ℝ) (hε0 : 0 ≤ ε) (hε1 : ε ≤ 1) (F : Finset ℤ) :
    ∑ p ∈ F, diffOp.apply (gE ε) p ^ 2 ≤ 8 := by
  have hT : ∀ p ∉ ({-1, 0, 1} : Finset ℤ), diffOp.apply (gE ε) p ^ 2 = 0 := by
    intro p hp
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton, not_or] at hp
    obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩ := hp
    have a1 : p + 1 ≠ 0 := by omega
    have a2 : p + 1 ≠ 1 := by omega
    rw [diffOp_apply]
    simp [gE, liftEx, bumpEx, a1, a2, h2, h3]
  refine (sum_le_of_vanish _ _ (fun p => sq_nonneg _) hT F).trans ?_
  simp [diffOp_apply, gE, liftEx, bumpEx]
  nlinarith

/-- **Witness for §2 with a varying sequence.** On `ℤ` with blocks `{2w, 2w + 1}`, the approximants
`g n = lift + (n + 1)⁻¹ · bump` are right inverses of the block averages for `y = δ₀` at every `n`, converge
pointwise to the block-constant lift, and have every finite window of their difference energy at most
`8`; the conclusions of `apply_eq_of_tendsto` and `energy_le_of_tendsto` follow for the limit. -/
theorem example_passage :
    (∀ i, Tendsto (fun n => gEx n i) atTop (𝓝 (liftEx i))) ∧
    (∀ k, ∀ᶠ n in atTop, blockAvg.apply (gEx n) k = (Finsupp.single (0 : ℤ) (1 : ℝ)) k) ∧
    (∀ F : Finset ℤ, ∀ᶠ n in atTop, ∑ p ∈ F, diffOp.apply (gEx n) p ^ 2 ≤ 8) ∧
    blockAvg.apply liftEx = ⇑(Finsupp.single (0 : ℤ) (1 : ℝ)) ∧
    (Summable (fun p => diffOp.apply liftEx p ^ 2) ∧ ∑' p, diffOp.apply liftEx p ^ 2 ≤ 8) := by
  have hA : ∀ k, ∀ᶠ n in atTop, blockAvg.apply (gEx n) k = (Finsupp.single (0 : ℤ) (1 : ℝ)) k :=
    fun k => Eventually.of_forall fun n => gE_blockAvg _ k
  have hE : ∀ F : Finset ℤ, ∀ᶠ n in atTop, ∑ p ∈ F, diffOp.apply (gEx n) p ^ 2 ≤ 8 := by
    intro F
    refine Eventually.of_forall fun n => gE_energy _ (by positivity) ?_ F
    rw [div_le_one (by positivity)]
    have := Nat.cast_nonneg (α := ℝ) n
    linarith
  exact ⟨gEx_tendsto, hA, hE, apply_eq_of_tendsto blockAvg gEx_tendsto _ hA,
    energy_le_of_tendsto diffOp gEx_tendsto 8 hE⟩

/-! ### The passage theorem on the identity lift -/

/-- The coarse energy on `ℤ`: `qK y = ∑' w, (y (w + 1) − y w)²`. -/
def qKEx (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) : ℝ := ∑' w, (y (w + 1) - y w) ^ 2

/-- The constant sequence of coercions `(ℤ →₀ ℝ) → (ℤ → ℝ)`. -/
def JnEx : ℕ → (ℤ →₀ ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (ℤ → ℝ) := fun _ => Finsupp.lcoeFun

/-- Each `JnEx n` is the coercion. -/
theorem JnEx_apply (n : ℕ) (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) : JnEx n y = ⇑y := rfl

/-- For finitely supported `y` on `ℤ`, `w ↦ (y (w + 1) − y w)²` is summable. -/
theorem summable_diff_sq (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) : Summable (fun w => (y (w + 1) - y w) ^ 2) := by
  classical
  refine summable_of_ne_finset_zero (s := y.support ∪ y.support.image (fun w => w - 1)) ?_
  intro w hw
  simp only [Finset.mem_union, Finset.mem_image, Finsupp.mem_support_iff, not_or, not_exists,
    not_and, ne_eq, not_not] at hw
  have h3 : y (w + 1) = 0 := by
    by_contra h
    exact hw.2 (w + 1) h (by ring)
  simp [hw.1, h3]

/-- Every finite window of `|δ_j|` has sum at most `1`. -/
theorem single_abs_sum_le (j : ℤ) (F : Finset ℤ) :
    ∑ i ∈ F, |(Finsupp.single j (1 : ℝ)) i| ≤ 1 := by
  have e : ∀ i, |(Finsupp.single j (1 : ℝ)) i| = if j = i then 1 else 0 := fun i => by
    rw [Finsupp.single_apply]
    split_ifs <;> simp
  simp_rw [e]
  rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq]
  split_ifs <;> norm_num

/-- **Witness for `lemmaJ_passage`** (degenerate: the sequence is constant and the lift is the identity).
On `ℤ`, with the identity as the block averages, the difference operator as the plaquette map,
`qK y = ∑' w, (y (w + 1) − y w)²`, `C = C1 = 1`, and `Jn n = J` the coercion of finitely supported fields,
the four hypotheses hold and the passage theorem gives its five conclusions. -/
theorem example_lemmaJ_passage :
    (∀ (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) (i : ℤ), Tendsto (fun n => JnEx n y i) atTop (𝓝 (y i))) ∧
    (∀ (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) (k : ℤ), ∀ᶠ n in atTop, idOp.apply (JnEx n y) k = y k) ∧
    (∀ (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) (F : Finset ℤ), ∀ᶠ n in atTop,
      ∑ p ∈ F, diffOp.apply (JnEx n y) p ^ 2 ≤ 1 ^ 2 * qKEx y) ∧
    (∀ (j : ℤ) (F : Finset ℤ), ∀ᶠ n in atTop,
      ∑ i ∈ F, |JnEx n (Finsupp.single j 1) i| ≤ 1) ∧
    (IsLinearMap ℝ (fun y : ℤ →₀ ℝ => (⇑y : ℤ → ℝ)) ∧
      (∀ y : ℤ →₀ ℝ, idOp.apply ⇑y = ⇑y) ∧
      (∀ y : ℤ →₀ ℝ, Summable (fun p => diffOp.apply ⇑y p ^ 2) ∧
        ∑' p, diffOp.apply ⇑y p ^ 2 ≤ 1 ^ 2 * qKEx y) ∧
      (∀ y : ℤ →₀ ℝ, Summable (fun i => |y i|) ∧ ∑' i, |y i| ≤ 1 * ∑ j ∈ y.support, |y j|) ∧
      (∀ y : ℤ →₀ ℝ, Summable (fun i => y i ^ 2) ∧
        ∑' i, y i ^ 2 ≤ (1 * ∑ j ∈ y.support, |y j|) ^ 2)) := by
  have hconv : ∀ (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) (i : ℤ), Tendsto (fun n => JnEx n y i) atTop (𝓝 (y i)) :=
    fun y i => tendsto_const_nhds
  have hA : ∀ (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) (k : ℤ), ∀ᶠ n in atTop, idOp.apply (JnEx n y) k = y k :=
    fun y k => Eventually.of_forall fun n => by rw [idOp_apply, JnEx_apply]
  have hD : ∀ (y : ℤ →₀ ℝ) (F : Finset ℤ), ∀ᶠ n in atTop,
      ∑ p ∈ F, diffOp.apply (JnEx n y) p ^ 2 ≤ 1 ^ 2 * qKEx y := by
    intro y F
    refine Eventually.of_forall fun n => ?_
    simp only [diffOp_apply, JnEx_apply, one_pow, one_mul, qKEx]
    exact (summable_diff_sq y).sum_le_tsum F (fun _ _ => sq_nonneg _)
  have hl1 : ∀ (j : ℤ) (F : Finset ℤ), ∀ᶠ n in atTop,
      ∑ i ∈ F, |JnEx n (Finsupp.single j 1) i| ≤ 1 :=
    fun j F => Eventually.of_forall fun n => by
      rw [JnEx_apply]
      exact single_abs_sum_le j F
  exact ⟨hconv, hA, hD, hl1,
    lemmaJ_passage idOp diffOp qKEx 1 1 JnEx (fun y => ⇑y) hconv hA hD hl1⟩

/-! ### Kernels, composition and the filter -/

/-- Column sums of `τ` as a local operator are at most `1`. -/
theorem tauOp_col (m : ℤ) (F : Finset ℤ) :
    ∑ i ∈ F.filter (fun i => m ∈ tauOp.supp i), |tauOp.coef i m| ≤ 1 := by
  have hsub : F.filter (fun i => m ∈ tauOp.supp i) ⊆ {m - 1, m, m + 1} := by
    intro i hi
    simp only [Finset.mem_filter, tauOp, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hi ⊢
    omega
  have h1 : m - 1 ∉ ({m, m + 1} : Finset ℤ) := by
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]
    omega
  have h2 : m ∉ ({m + 1} : Finset ℤ) := by
    simp only [Finset.mem_singleton]
    omega
  have e1 : m ≠ m - 1 := by omega
  have e2 : m ≠ m + 1 := by omega
  calc ∑ i ∈ F.filter (fun i => m ∈ tauOp.supp i), |tauOp.coef i m|
        ≤ ∑ i ∈ ({m - 1, m, m + 1} : Finset ℤ), |tauOp.coef i m| :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg hsub fun _ _ _ => abs_nonneg _
    _ = 1 := by
        rw [Finset.sum_insert h1, Finset.sum_insert h2, Finset.sum_singleton]
        simp only [tauOp, if_neg e1, if_neg e2]
        norm_num

/-- Column sums of the translation kernel `(m, j) ↦ g (m − j)` on `ℤ` are at most `2`. -/
theorem gk_col (j : ℤ) (F : Finset ℤ) : ∑ m ∈ F, |gk (m - j)| ≤ 2 := by
  have hinj : Set.InjOn (fun m : ℤ => m - j) F := fun a _ b _ h => sub_left_injective h
  have h := sum_abs_gk_le (F.image (fun m => m - j))
  rwa [Finset.sum_image hinj] at h

/-- The composite kernel of `τ` with `(m, j) ↦ g (m − j)` is the identity kernel. -/
theorem tauOp_gk (i j : ℤ) : tauOp.apply (fun m => gk (m - j)) i = if i = j then 1 else 0 := by
  rw [tauOp_apply]
  have e1 : i - 1 - j = (i - j) - 1 := by ring
  have e2 : i + 1 - j = (i - j) + 1 := by ring
  have h : tau (fun m => gk (m - j)) i = tau gk (i - j) := by
    simp only [tau, e1, e2]
  rw [h, tau_gk]
  by_cases hij : i = j
  · simp [hij]
  · have hne : i - j ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.mpr hij
    simp [hij, hne]

/-- **Witness for `comp_column_bound`.** The filter `τ` on `ℤ` (a local operator with column sums `1`)
composed with the kernel `(m, j) ↦ g (m − j)` (column sums `2`) has column sums at most `1 · 2`; the
composite is in fact the identity kernel, since `τ g = δ₀`. -/
theorem example_comp_column :
    (∀ (m : ℤ) (F : Finset ℤ), ∑ i ∈ F.filter (fun i => m ∈ tauOp.supp i), |tauOp.coef i m| ≤ 1) ∧
    (∀ (j : ℤ) (F : Finset ℤ), ∑ m ∈ F, |gk (m - j)| ≤ 2) ∧
    (∀ (j : ℤ) (F : Finset ℤ), ∑ i ∈ F, |tauOp.apply (fun m => gk (m - j)) i| ≤ 1 * 2) ∧
    (∀ i j : ℤ, tauOp.apply (fun m => gk (m - j)) i = if i = j then 1 else 0) :=
  ⟨tauOp_col, gk_col,
    fun j F => comp_column_bound tauOp (fun m j => gk (m - j)) 1 2 zero_le_one tauOp_col gk_col j F,
    tauOp_gk⟩

/-- The unit field at the origin of `ℤ⁴`. -/
def y0 : Z4 →₀ ℝ := Finsupp.single 0 1

/-- `∑ |y0| = 1`. -/
theorem y0_abs_sum : ∑ z' ∈ y0.support, |y0 z'| = 1 := by
  simp [y0]

/-- `∑ y0² = 1`. -/
theorem y0_sq_sum : ∑ z' ∈ y0.support, y0 z' ^ 2 = 1 := by
  simp [y0]

/-- **Witness for §3 and §5 on `ℤ⁴`.** The right-inverse kernel `G` of the filter: `τ g = δ₀`, `∑ |g| = 2`,
`T G = δ₀`, `|G z| = 4 s^{|z|₁}`, and the translation kernel `G (z − z')` has row and column sums at most
`16`; for the unit field `y0` at the origin this gives `T (G ∗ y0) = y0`, `∑' |G ∗ y0| ≤ 16` and
`∑' (G ∗ y0)² ≤ 256`. -/
theorem example_filter :
    (∀ j, tau gk j = if j = 0 then 1 else 0) ∧ HasSum (fun j : ℤ => |gk j|) 2 ∧
    (∀ z, Tf Gk z = if z = 0 then 1 else 0) ∧
    (∀ z, |Gk z| = 4 * sdec ^ (∑ ν, (z ν).natAbs)) ∧
    (∀ (z' : Z4) (F : Finset Z4), ∑ z ∈ F, |Gk (z - z')| ≤ 16) ∧
    (∀ (z : Z4) (S : Finset Z4), ∑ z' ∈ S, |Gk (z - z')| ≤ 16) ∧
    Tf (Gconv y0) = ⇑y0 ∧
    (Summable (fun z => |Gconv y0 z|) ∧ ∑' z, |Gconv y0 z| ≤ 16) ∧
    (Summable (fun z => Gconv y0 z ^ 2) ∧ ∑' z, Gconv y0 z ^ 2 ≤ 256) := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := Gconv_l1 y0
  obtain ⟨h3, h4⟩ := Gconv_l2 y0
  rw [y0_abs_sum, mul_one] at h2
  rw [y0_sq_sum, mul_one] at h4
  norm_num at h4
  exact ⟨tau_gk, hasSum_abs_gk, Tf_Gk, abs_Gk, sum_abs_Gk_sub_le, sum_abs_Gk_sub_le',
    Tf_Gconv y0, ⟨h1, h2⟩, ⟨h3, h4⟩⟩

/-- **Witness for the `ℓ¹` Fatou bound and for `summable_sq_of_summable_abs`.** The kernels
`(1 − (n + 1)⁻¹) g` converge pointwise to `g` and have every finite window of `ℓ¹` mass at most `2`; hence
`∑' |g| ≤ 2` and `∑' g² ≤ 4`. -/
theorem example_fatou_l1 :
    (∀ i : ℤ, Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => (1 - 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1)) * gk i) atTop (𝓝 (gk i))) ∧
    (∀ F : Finset ℤ, ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, ∑ i ∈ F, |(1 - 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1)) * gk i| ≤ 2) ∧
    ((∀ F : Finset ℤ, ∑ i ∈ F, |gk i| ≤ 2) ∧ Summable (fun i => |gk i|) ∧ ∑' i, |gk i| ≤ 2) ∧
    (Summable (fun i => gk i ^ 2) ∧ ∑' i, gk i ^ 2 ≤ 4) := by
  have hconv : ∀ i : ℤ, Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => (1 - 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1)) * gk i) atTop (𝓝 (gk i)) := by
    intro i
    have h := (tendsto_const_nhds (x := (1 : ℝ))).sub (tendsto_one_div_add_atTop_nhds_zero_nat (𝕜 := ℝ))
    simpa using h.mul_const (gk i)
  have hB : ∀ F : Finset ℤ, ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, ∑ i ∈ F, |(1 - 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1)) * gk i| ≤ 2 := by
    intro F
    refine Eventually.of_forall fun n => ?_
    have hk : (0 : ℝ) < (n : ℝ) + 1 := by positivity
    have h0 : 0 ≤ 1 - 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1) := by
      rw [sub_nonneg, div_le_one hk]
      have := Nat.cast_nonneg (α := ℝ) n
      linarith
    have h1 : 1 - 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1) ≤ 1 := by
      have : 0 ≤ 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1) := by positivity
      linarith
    calc ∑ i ∈ F, |(1 - 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1)) * gk i| ≤ ∑ i ∈ F, |gk i| := by
          refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun i _ => ?_
          rw [abs_mul, abs_of_nonneg h0]
          exact mul_le_of_le_one_left (abs_nonneg _) h1
      _ ≤ 2 := sum_abs_gk_le F
  have hl := l1_le_of_tendsto hconv 2 hB
  obtain ⟨hs2, hle2⟩ := summable_sq_of_summable_abs hl.2.1
  refine ⟨hconv, hB, hl, hs2, hle2.trans ?_⟩
  rw [hasSum_abs_gk.tsum_eq]
  norm_num

/-- **Witness for `recovery_of_lift`.** In `ℝ × ℝ` with `M` the first projection: `e j = ((j + 1)⁻¹, 1) →
(0, 1)`, `M (0, 1) = 0`, and `c j = ((j + 1)⁻¹, 0)` has `M (c j) = M (e j)` and `‖c j‖ ≤ 1 · ‖M (e j)‖`;
then `e j − c j = (0, 1)` lies in `ker M` and converges to `(0, 1)`. -/
theorem example_recovery :
    Tendsto (fun j : ℕ => ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ))) atTop (𝓝 ((0 : ℝ), (1 : ℝ))) ∧
    ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ ((0 : ℝ), (1 : ℝ)) = 0 ∧
    (∀ j : ℕ, ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (0 : ℝ)) =
      ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ))) ∧
    (∀ j : ℕ, ‖((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (0 : ℝ))‖ ≤
      1 * ‖ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ))‖) ∧
    ((∀ j : ℕ, ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ
        (((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ)) - ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (0 : ℝ))) = 0) ∧
      Tendsto (fun j : ℕ => ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ)) - ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (0 : ℝ)))
        atTop (𝓝 ((0 : ℝ), (1 : ℝ)))) := by
  have he : Tendsto (fun j : ℕ => ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ))) atTop (𝓝 ((0 : ℝ), (1 : ℝ))) :=
    (tendsto_one_div_add_atTop_nhds_zero_nat (𝕜 := ℝ)).prodMk_nhds tendsto_const_nhds
  have hM0 : ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ ((0 : ℝ), (1 : ℝ)) = 0 := rfl
  have hMc : ∀ j : ℕ, ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (0 : ℝ)) =
      ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ)) := fun j => rfl
  have hc : ∀ j : ℕ, ‖((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (0 : ℝ))‖ ≤
      1 * ‖ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ))‖ := fun j => by
    simp [Prod.norm_def]
  exact ⟨he, hM0, hMc, hc, recovery_of_lift (ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ) 1
    (fun j : ℕ => ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (1 : ℝ)))
    (fun j : ℕ => ((1 : ℝ) / ((j : ℝ) + 1), (0 : ℝ))) _ he hM0 hMc hc⟩

/-- **Witness for §1.** Block averages read only their block; the composite of the block averages with
the difference operator is the composite of their actions, and its output index `w` reads only the
fine sites `2w, 2w + 1, 2w + 2`. -/
theorem example_locality :
    (∀ (k : ℤ) (f g : ℤ → ℝ), (∀ i ∈ blockAvg.supp k, f i = g i) →
      blockAvg.apply f k = blockAvg.apply g k) ∧
    (∀ f : ℤ → ℝ, (blockAvg.comp diffOp).apply f = blockAvg.apply (diffOp.apply f)) ∧
    (∀ w i : ℤ, i ∈ (blockAvg.comp diffOp).supp w → 2 * w ≤ i ∧ i ≤ 2 * w + 2) := by
  refine ⟨fun k f g h => blockAvg.apply_congr k h, fun f => LocalOp.comp_apply _ _ f, ?_⟩
  intro w i hi
  simp only [LocalOp.comp, blockAvg, diffOp, Finset.mem_biUnion, Finset.mem_insert,
    Finset.mem_singleton] at hi
  obtain ⟨a, ha, hia⟩ := hi
  omega

end Example

